00:33:55.520 --> 00:33:59.210
So we were talking previously
about how Postgres now

00:33:59.210 --> 00:34:02.000
has high-availability
capabilities where

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:03.020
it didn't before.

00:34:03.020 --> 00:34:05.420
But the question is,
how do I actually

00:34:05.420 --> 00:34:07.770
go about setting that up?

00:34:07.770 --> 00:34:09.989
It's actually really
straightforward.

00:34:09.989 --> 00:34:10.790
There are APIs.

00:34:10.790 --> 00:34:12.320
But the simplest
way is basically

00:34:12.320 --> 00:34:15.290
going into your Cloud
SQL instances page.

00:34:15.290 --> 00:34:18.310
You'll see now that there is
a high-availability regional

00:34:18.310 --> 00:34:19.310
checkbox.

00:34:19.310 --> 00:34:21.080
That will be under
your instance.

00:34:21.080 --> 00:34:23.264
It doesn't have to
be an old instance.

00:34:23.264 --> 00:34:24.889
You can create a
whole new one as well.

00:34:24.889 --> 00:34:26.555
But basically, there's
a checkbox there.

00:34:26.555 --> 00:34:27.429
You turn it on.

00:34:27.429 --> 00:34:29.500
Enable auto backups
and high availability.

00:34:29.500 --> 00:34:30.290
Click Save.

00:34:30.290 --> 00:34:33.230
And you are pretty
much good to go.

00:34:33.230 --> 00:34:34.969
What's also really
nice about this

00:34:34.969 --> 00:34:38.179
is if you want to test what
happens when, say, failover

00:34:38.179 --> 00:34:40.070
happens, so your
database goes down,

00:34:40.070 --> 00:34:43.156
and it flips over to the backup,
there is a gcloud as well as

00:34:43.156 --> 00:34:44.750
an API that you can call.

00:34:44.750 --> 00:34:47.750
Basically, you can call
gcloud SQL instances failover.

00:34:47.750 --> 00:34:51.050
And that will take down
your primary instance

00:34:51.050 --> 00:34:53.037
and then flail you
over to your secondary.

00:34:53.037 --> 00:34:54.620
And then you'll be
able to see exactly

00:34:54.620 --> 00:34:55.730
what your application's doing.

00:34:55.730 --> 00:34:56.960
This is probably
something you want

00:34:56.960 --> 00:34:58.340
to do while everyone's
sitting around,

00:34:58.340 --> 00:35:00.140
rather than at 3
o'clock in the morning

00:35:00.140 --> 00:35:02.780
if something goes wrong so that
you can move ahead and see what

00:35:02.780 --> 00:35:03.700
happens.

00:35:03.700 --> 00:35:04.720
MELANIE WARRICK: Nice.

